# Create a New Doxia Module

First, the easiest way is to create a POM with _doxia-modules_ as parent:

```xml
<project>
  <parent>
    <groupId>org.apache.maven.doxia</groupId>
    <artifactId>doxia-modules</artifactId>
    <version>${doxiaVersion}</version> <!-- Latest release -->
  </parent>
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
  <artifactId>doxia-module-my</artifactId>
  <name>Doxia :: MY Module</name>

  ...
</project>
```

Secondly, you should implement some Doxia classes, depending on what features you want: parsing or generating markup. Parsers, parser modules and sink factories are JSR-330 components, named by `@Named`; the _doxia-modules_ parent already writes the component index. For details, see [Maven & JSR-330](/maven-jsr330.html#How_to_name_components).

${esc.h}${esc.h} Parsing

- _MyParser_ class

    ```java
    import javax.inject.Named;
    import javax.inject.Singleton;
    
    import org.apache.maven.doxia.parser.AbstractParser;
    
    @Singleton
    @Named("my")
    public class MyParser
        extends AbstractParser
    {
    ...
    }
    ```

    Depending on the type markup, extending `AbstractTextParser`, `AbstractXmlParser` or `Xhtml5BaseParser` may give you more features.

- _MyParseException_ class (optional)

    ```java
    import org.apache.maven.doxia.parser.ParseException;
    
    public class MyParseException
        extends ParseException
    {
    ...
    }
    ```

- _MyParserModule_ class

    ```java
    import javax.inject.Named;
    import javax.inject.Singleton;
    
    import org.apache.maven.doxia.parser.module.AbstractParserModule;
    
    @Singleton
    @Named("my")
    public class MyParserModule
        extends AbstractParserModule
    {
    ...
    }
    ```

${esc.h}${esc.h} Generating

- _MySink_ class

    ```java
    import org.apache.maven.doxia.sink.impl.SinkAdapter;
    
    public class MySink
        extends SinkAdapter
    {
    ...
    }
    ```

    Depending on the type markup, extending `AbstractTextSink`, `AbstractXmlSink` or `Xhtml5BaseSink` may give you more features.

- _MySinkFactory_ class

    ```java
    import javax.inject.Named;
    import javax.inject.Singleton;
    
    import org.apache.maven.doxia.sink.SinkFactory;
    
    @Singleton
    @Named("my")
    public class MySinkFactory
        implements SinkFactory
    {
    ...
    }
    ```

    Depending on the type markup, extending `AbstractTextSinkFactory` or `AbstractXmlSinkFactory` may give you more features.

